 in Diagram II is not a subspace of ${R}^{3}.$\n\n- Diagram III represents the origin $0=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\,,\\,$ which is considered a special (trivial) subspace of ${R}^{3}.$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186347509 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e3fe3596-340e-5155-bed3-cf25f5843d70" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Whether Sets Represented Graphically Are Subspaces in Two-Dimensional Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c28fd393-ff65-5692-b81c-16220b5bd950" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347511} {:answer/id #uuid "88de2e77-1ff6-5160-96bc-1f5c496449a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347512} {:answer/id #uuid "8bf463be-34db-5d32-9b3e-48b71b12f473" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347513} {:answer/id #uuid "d2ad0273-6487-5ef4-8d05-d33b21c3afe4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347514} {:answer/id #uuid "a8807478-a217-5b90-a6b4-ac1cc710bc25" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347515}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "88de2e77-1ff6-5160-96bc-1f5c496449a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347512} :answer-field/id #uuid "e6ec6134-c0a6-5fd7-b801-817329cfaebb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347510}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "221a2198-53b2-56e9-a191-c3049ddc3afe" :question/math-academy-id "q-34174" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045249/assets/d4bd3b326c89316bc916658421bcd4c65c32a72672af9fbd7aa5397cb53ab374.png)\n\nWhich of the diagrams shown above represent subspaces of ${R}^{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each diagram in turn.\n\n- Diagram I does not represent a subspace. The vector $a=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ lies inside the given subset. But \n\n$$\n(-1)\\cdot a=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nlies outside the subset.\n\n- Diagram II does not represent a subspace. The vector $a=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$  lies inside the given subset. But\n\n$$\n(-1)\\cdot a=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nlies outside the subset.\n\n- Diagram III represents a subspace. It represents the whole plane, which is considered a special subspace of ${R}^{2}.$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186347516 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4a8dbbab-2dea-5fff-86f0-3411f5405ee9" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Whether Sets Represented Graphically Are Subspaces in Three-Dimensional Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e82f5a28-ee87-526a-aae8-0a4f041a4194" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347518} {:answer/id #uuid "9cdc6728-ce16-5de3-8c09-b889680b8321" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347519} {:answer/id #uuid "632724b2-8973-54aa-950b-ee6bc2dbb0d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347520} {:answer/id #uuid "77feca6e-4e30-54d1-830f-6a01f5c791dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347521} {:answer/id #uuid "70f3d8a9-0ea3-51df-9808-575bcb1d1838" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347522}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "70f3d8a9-0ea3-